The useful rule is not that every crude project hides a billion-dollar sequel. The rule is narrower: $\text{failed first product}
\;\not\Longrightarrow\;
\text{failed founder}.$ The founder can be wrong at the level of the first product and still be right at the level of the deeper entrepreneurial motion.

